From: Zheng Zhang <everything411@qq.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: normalize undefined QCN9074 board id

QCN9074 firmware 2.15.x reports 0xffffffff when no board id is defined,
while ath11k uses 0xff for that case. This makes the driver generate a
board name with qmi-board-id=-1 and the board file lookup fails with:

  failed to fetch board data for bus=pci,qmi-chip-id=0,qmi-board-id=-1

Convert only this QCN9074 sentinel to 0xff. Do not mask every board id,
because the QMI field is u32 and valid ids may use bits above bit 7.

Signed-off-by: Zheng Zhang <everything411@qq.com>
Link: https://github.com/mirror/dd-wrt/commit/b9b601e8aa4a9dbc66cbc4c946f42114fa10260f
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/qmi.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/qmi.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/qmi.c
@@ -2267,6 +2267,11 @@ static int ath11k_qmi_request_target_cap
 	else
 		ab->qmi.target.board_id = 0xFF;
 
+	/* QCN9074 firmware 2.15.x uses 0xffffffff for an undefined board id. */
+	if (ab->hw_rev == ATH11K_HW_QCN9074_HW10 &&
+	    ab->qmi.target.board_id == 0xffffffff)
+		ab->qmi.target.board_id = 0xFF;
+
 	if (resp.soc_info_valid)
 		ab->qmi.target.soc_id = resp.soc_info.soc_id;
 
